#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b838ae03-e4f7-5c50-87e2-7260f30d319f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.857\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338267} {:answer/id #uuid "58dfb56d-151a-532b-8c17-cf232edca91f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.434\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338268} {:answer/id #uuid "e9aa5602-f788-5169-8420-a93fecc21a78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.927\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338269} {:answer/id #uuid "e57c74f7-c19c-56c9-aa41-000a8cdbf6fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338270} {:answer/id #uuid "32bed052-5197-5377-ab64-ca0154770811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.927\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e57c74f7-c19c-56c9-aa41-000a8cdbf6fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338270} :answer-field/id #uuid "48256dd1-ac87-57fa-99ee-1cf29bdfd76f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6adea076-135d-565e-9953-1bbd05568820" :question/math-academy-id "q-17519" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-4-3\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})| \\\\  & ≈\\pi +0.643\\,50… \\\\  & ≈3.785.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=5$ and $\\theta =3.785$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\,\\text{i}}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9284b0a5-6797-5f77-b7a1-d4c0b8fe315e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.389\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338274} {:answer/id #uuid "027c16c5-2973-5717-8af4-0135a10f6020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338275} {:answer/id #uuid "76927f0f-078b-5d44-88fa-aa29a676241c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338276} {:answer/id #uuid "274fc05d-1f82-55d1-bec8-b925b6291c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338277} {:answer/id #uuid "42cfe6cd-8c70-5046-b98e-d974d4d8aea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.983\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76927f0f-078b-5d44-88fa-aa29a676241c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338276} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5df713a-1952-5f2f-aad9-fbc435f9cd6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a435c59-9a38-57a4-9c2b-af498b51b708" :question/math-academy-id "q-17524" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-2+6\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-3)| \\\\  & ≈1.893.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =1.893$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93831ade-92f3-55a1-898c-1fa9b3e39dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2\\sqrt{3}e^{π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086318} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7fafd2-561e-57cf-b458-6ac7b266706e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{5π\\textrm{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086319} {:answer/id #uuid "12a1c4f6-c394-5811-bf5c-ec8f6641bd82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 3e^{3π\\textrm{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086320} {:answer/id #uuid "2c382927-796b-5057-a3b3-9cad5a5084cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 3\\sqrt{2}e^{π\\textrm{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086321} {:answer/id #uuid "363041ed-687c-5519-803b-30905ceab477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "363041ed-687c-5519-803b-30905ceab477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086322} :answer-field/id #uuid "1736925a-0723-5e18-b493-5324e70cc51b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "145945c1-66ab-5fe7-89d2-3b7864c48fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71978" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/c5d36b72e7e2ff6754152a559d64bf3610708c9a2d3790c859bc9abacc9220b6.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a238e508-9d15-5832-b53e-947a4e50073d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338281} {:answer/id #uuid "0d33b851-6ffa-5aec-8c8b-e53bd46e586a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338282} {:answer/id #uuid "2e7c41b7-1dc1-5c34-9e4e-933e5b3be622" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338283} {:answer/id #uuid "2f71b7b8-7466-52bf-b9fd-cf845143c794" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338284} {:answer/id #uuid "2e52a703-3688-5feb-9014-4b2a260e5a06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e52a703-3688-5feb-9014-4b2a260e5a06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338285} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9651cee-cfac-5a7f-beb7-821a6a9f1e80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "389cf7b9-2b41-57c8-80f6-0da73021dc80" :question/math-academy-id "q-8079" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=1-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d76815-e545-5a1f-9d74-b0e8cecf03a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338288} {:answer/id #uuid "f8abc44d-ee07-51c8-9c53-d20b91d260ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.245\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338289} {:answer/id #uuid "99526b05-742a-5fbd-8bee-3357e41f8e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.245\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338290} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6e3183-a89b-501c-8369-4e91fb88c6a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338291} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8a88c7-1663-5d9a-b467-98dae17d77ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b6e3183-a89b-501c-8369-4e91fb88c6a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338291} :answer-field/id #uuid "60730ae9-03c9-5d8b-b308-95618926d721" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6442ed14-04ef-564f-83f4-3a6e00a9f925" :question/math-academy-id "q-8083" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/83c490278bec718da1338f8926e9d67d2f72909487b9a85bbd386cbf72def2bb.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-4+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{4})| \\\\  & ≈2.897.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\theta =2.897$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}]}
